[118.752613, "i", "cat >> README.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Webhook authentication and outage recovery\n\nWebhook requests always require a valid, current `Paygate-Signature`; replay-token\nheaders do not bypass verification. During secret rotation, any configured signing\nsecret may match any supplied `v1` signature. Verified retries are deduplicated by\n`event_id`, including ignored events, without rewriting stored payloads or auditing again.\n\nFor trusted outage payloads already stored in `ops/backlog/`, use:\n\n    npm run replay-backlog\n\nThis local recovery tool skips processed event IDs and obeys the refund-storm guard\nin `config/refunds.json`: at most 20 events per run, at least 120 seconds between runs.\nRepeat after the required interval until it reports zero remaining events; do not\nrelax the guard to drain a backlog. Internal HTTP replay still requires a bearer key\nwith `refunds:replay` permission.\nEOF\ngit --no-pager diff --check\n"]
[118.752973, "o", "cat >> README.md <<'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[118.753335, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Webhook authentication and outage recovery\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
